;; og:preserve-this runtime-link guard (forge #219, class sweep alongside 693f31412):
;; every set! below writes through *speech-control* unconditionally at top level the
;; instant this file links. *speech-control* is (the-as speech-control #f) until
;; something allocates a real instance (speech-h.gc:185), so each set! computes a
;; field address from a null base and writes through it, silently corrupting memory
;; near address 0 rather than faulting immediately; this is the SIG-A mechanism, not
;; SIG-B's immediate null jump. One guard covers the whole block since every form here
;; targets the same global. Retires when *speech-control* is landed as a real instance
;; before this file's DGO links.
